e our work and share it with  others  so that's where our final product comes  in our studio connect and this is a  server that allows you to automate your  processes and what's really cool is that  from a repositories and Azure devops we  can deploy our work into our studio  connect  and from connect we can automate data  processing we can schedule reports  and we can post shiny apps  so RCA connect provided us more  processing power which allowed us to do  analyzes more quickly so just as an  example this is one of our servers we  have about 251 gigabytes of RAM which is  a lot or another example the amount of  CPU queries available and we have a  number of these servers available to us  to do different types of data processing  or host apps and I can can't explain the  giddiness I felt the first time I ran a  script on connect that took 10 minutes  when it used to take over an hour to run  if it didn't crash so connect was a  really great life saver in terms of  finishing or data processing in more  quickly quick manner allowing me to go  to sleep earlier  so it's not only quicker but it also  feed up our hands at least in our  environment we're limited to two  workbenches so it's kind of like having  two our consoles or two tabs and if I  have many types of data that I need to  process throughout the week it's as if  my hands are tied so by being able to  offset it off to a server I can free up  my hands to do other type of work  and we can schedule jobs on the server  I'm using for example the officer or  open xlsx package to make PowerPoints  Excel sheets or Word Documents  um in that same theater processing we  can also be doing the data the large  amount of data processing and then  creating reports that are outputted at a  scheduled time  and we can schedule emails with the  Blaster package and a couple emails here  and there is not too bad but when we  start to you need to share your emails  and data with a lot of different  partners this becomes a really great  tool to use  and here's one example of data that we  put on the website weekly for post  vaccination infection data if you want  to check it out and all of this data is  processed via connect and then shared  with our partners at cdpage to later  publish on the website  so we can kind of think of connect as if  they're replacing this they're robots  they're running in their own lane and  they're running their own processes  and it's at this point I might want to  sit back and look at my cat and listen  to her and stop looking at this monitor  but in reality automation isn't perfect  and it often actually fails and can be  quite challenging to debug I'm working  on a server the debugging process is a  lot different the logs are different so  we we tried to so we need to think about  that as well so in reality it's more  like this we're all running in the same  Lane some of the processes are falling  over I'm falling over Etc  and one of the solutions to this is was  to create a data processing monitoring  app so this monitors all of our  processes on connect and it gives us a  really great visualization of what's  occurring and when it might fail  and in addition to that we have an error  logging system where if something breaks  we get an email via blastula telling us  something's broken and where in that  script it broke so I don't have time to  share that with you right now but if  you're interested and there's actually a  talk by my colleagues Colby Parish Andy  fan coming up next that you can check  out to see that specific piece of our  workflow  and then lastly we have many different  chatting apps mostly internal that I  can't share with you but one of those  published to the public by the  California covid-19 modeling team called  Calcutt and this shows you the current  state and predicted feature State using  different models of covid-19 in the  state of California so encourage you to  check this out and see the different  types of data that we're working with  and what's I think really cool is that  you can download the data as well that  we've all been processing and that's  updated regularly  so this gives you a very high level  overview of the different tools that we  use to create this workflow using Azure  devops RSV workbench and our studio  connect allowing us to process data in a  very quick amount of time and freeing up  our hands to make products that help  guide decision making in the state of  where to allocate resources  so thank you all for your time and  special thanks to data processing and  informatics section for all our homework  [Applause]  [Music]


